# hum.thrum — the thrum, hum's vibration protocol, in one file.
#
# A tone is one vibration: a chi from the range below, the body that chi
# declares, and the envelope every tone carries. A bee sounds a tone and
# humd carries it to whoever is tuned to hear it. Nothing here names a
# socket, a pipe or a peer: those are media a tone travels through, each
# bound in THRUM.md, and the tone is the same in all of them.
#
# One declaration per line, KEYWORD first. A DOC line documents the line
# above it. A blank line is nothing; a line starting with # is a comment.
#
#   THRUM <version>                the range's version
#   ENVELOPE                       what every tone carries
#   CHI <name>                     one vibration in the range
#     EMITS <party>..              who sounds it: a role, bee (any role), or humd
#     HEARS <party>..              who it is for
#     CARRIES ensemble             it may cross between humds
#   SHAPE <name>                   a shape nested in a body, not a chi of its own
#   KIND <name>                    a closed set of strings
#     VALUE <name>                 one of them
#   FIELD <key> <type>             a wire key and its type; a trailing ? means optional
#   PATTERN <name>                 tones that make one figure
#     KEY <field>                  what its tones share; the connection when absent
#     OPEN / STEP / CLOSE <chi>..  how it opens, grows and closes
#   ADVISORY <code>                what the thrum tells a bee to fix, without refusing it
#     BY <client|humd>..           who raises it
#
# Types: string, bool, int, uint, float, any; [t] a list of t; {t} a map
# of t keyed by string; a KIND or a SHAPE by its name; chi, a chi of this
# range.
#
# For what a tone is, this file wins: thrum-core's Rust is held to it,
# the TS, Python, Go and C clients are emitted from it, and THRUM.md's
# tables are read out of it. For what a party does with a tone, THRUM.md
# wins.

THRUM 0.8.0

ENVELOPE
DOC what every tone carries, whatever its chi
FIELD chi chi
DOC which vibration this is
FIELD rid string
DOC the echo key: an echo, or a reply, carries the rid of what it answers; never a dedup key
FIELD from string?
DOC who sounded it: a humd's hid in hex when crossing humds, a bee's name on a local socket
FIELD to string?
DOC the humd it is for, in hex; absent when it stays local
FIELD sigil string?
DOC the 12-character hash of the sid, stable across reconnects
FIELD sid string?
DOC the line of blooms it belongs to; the forager picks it
FIELD wane uint?
DOC its place in its sigil's order: a Lamport clock, one per sigil
FIELD sentAt int?
DOC when it was sounded, wall-clock ms, UTC
FIELD dusk int?
DOC when it fades, absolute ms: a tone arriving past it is dropped before anything else is checked
FIELD mid string?
DOC heard at most once: a receiver that has already dispatched this mid drops the repeat
FIELD ext {{any}}?
DOC a bee's own data under its own key, carried untouched

# The range. A chi's EMITS and HEARS are the roles' sends and receives:
# direction is sacred, and a role keeps to it for the whole of its life.

CHI hello
DOC announce self: hive, role, signed identity
EMITS bee
HEARS humd
FIELD protoVersion string
DOC the THRUM version the bee speaks; another major is refused, another minor advised
FIELD hive string
DOC the hive the bee belongs to; it must be installed on the humd
FIELD role role
DOC the one job it was entered for
FIELD builds bool?
DOC a forager whose blooms build where it is
FIELD version string?
DOC the bee's own version, semver
FIELD hid string
DOC who the bee is: the hash of its key
FIELD pubkey string
DOC the bee's ed25519 public key, hex
FIELD signedAt int
DOC when it signed, ms UTC; a stale signature is refused
FIELD signature string
DOC over hid and signedAt, from the key that hashes to hid
FIELD models [string]?
DOC a nurse: the models it grows; an attendant: the models it distils a scent of
FIELD tools [any]?
DOC an attendant: the fixed, named tools it serves
FIELD chis [string]?
DOC the chi values the bee speaks
FIELD propensity any?
DOC the bee's typology: statefulness, richness, wire
FIELD headroom headroom?
DOC a nurse: how many more cells it can take
FIELD source string?
DOC where the bee's source lives, a URL
FIELD bind any?
DOC an address the bee may be reached at, for the ensemble's manifest of it

CHI prompt
DOC open a bloom: its petals, the blooms before it, and how the cell should grow it
EMITS forager
HEARS nurse
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD modelId string?
DOC the model to grow it; any nurse with room, growing with a model of its own, when absent
FIELD cwd string?
DOC where the bloom builds: hum://<humdid>/<path>
FIELD systemPrompt string?
DOC the words the cell is given before the bloom's
FIELD text string?
DOC the words, when the bloom is only words
FIELD content [petal]?
DOC the petals the bloom opens with
FIELD tools [any]?
DOC the tools the bloom may reach; humd fills it before a nurse sees it
FIELD allowedTools [string]?
DOC of those, the names the bloom may use; all when absent
FIELD resume string?
DOC a cell's own session to grow on, where the hive keeps one
FIELD temperature float?
DOC how warm the sampling is
FIELD prune prune?
DOC cut the unlikely tail
FIELD season uint?
DOC how many tokens the bloom may grow
FIELD frost [string]?
DOC where the bloom stops
FIELD seed int?
DOC a seed, for a bloom grown again the same
FIELD trellis any?
DOC the shape the answer grows along: a schema, or "json"
FIELD tendrils tendrils?
DOC how the bloom reaches its tendrils
FIELD sepal sepal?
DOC how much the cell reasons first
FIELD scion string?
DOC the text that comes after the bloom: it grows what joins where it starts to this
FIELD graft [bloom]?
DOC the blooms of its sigil before it, oldest first, for a cell that did not grow them

CHI cancel
DOC stop the open bloom
EMITS forager
HEARS nurse
CARRIES ensemble

CHI cleanup
DOC drop humd's state for a sigil
EMITS forager
HEARS nurse builder
CARRIES ensemble

CHI curate
DOC manual compaction request
EMITS forager
HEARS nurse

CHI scout-result
DOC a scout came back
EMITS forager
HEARS nurse
FIELD callId string?
DOC the scout it answers
FIELD output any?
DOC what it brought back

CHI tendril-result
DOC what a tendril grasped
EMITS forager builder attendant
HEARS nurse forager
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD callId string
DOC the reach it answers
FIELD output string?
DOC what it grasped, as text
FIELD result any?
DOC what it grasped, as JSON
FIELD isError bool?
DOC the grasp failed, and output or result says why
FIELD title string?
DOC a line to show for the grasp
FIELD metadata any?
DOC what else it carries: exitCode on a bash grasp

CHI breath
DOC accept a hello, and keep the bee in step
EMITS humd
HEARS bee
FIELD sigils any
DOC state per sigil, usually {}; [] on the breath humd gives before it has heard anything, which admits nothing
FIELD protoVersion string?
DOC the THRUM version humd speaks
FIELD models [model]?
DOC for a forager: the models nurses grow
FIELD scents [model]?
DOC for a forager: the scents attendants distil
FIELD tools [any]?
DOC for a forager: the tools attendants serve its blooms

CHI unfurl
DOC a petal growing
EMITS nurse
HEARS forager
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD petal uint
DOC its index in the bloom
FIELD kind petal-kind
DOC which unit of content is growing
FIELD text string?
DOC words: of a text, sepal or thorn petal
FIELD sap string?
DOC a tendril's input, as it grows
FIELD callId string?
DOC of a tendril petal: the reach it opens
FIELD name string?
DOC of a tendril petal: the tool
FIELD grain grain?
DOC of a pollen petal
FIELD propolis string?
DOC sealing a sepal petal, so it can carry into the next bloom
FIELD source any?
DOC of a waggle petal: where the words came from
FIELD brix any?
DOC of a brix petal: how likely each token was
FIELD closed bool?
DOC once the petal is whole

CHI wilt
DOC close the bloom, with its nectar
EMITS nurse
HEARS forager
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD reason string
DOC stop; max_tokens when its season ran out; refusal; cancel; or the cell's own word
FIELD nectar any?
DOC what the bloom took: tokens in and out, cache reads and writes
FIELD exitCode int?
DOC the cell process's exit code, when it had one
FIELD subtype string?
DOC the cell's own word for how it closed

CHI error
DOC the bloom broke off
EMITS nurse attendant humd
HEARS forager
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD message string
DOC what broke
FIELD code string?
DOC no-nurse when no nurse here or on a trusted peer grows the model; nurse-gone from humd when the peer growing it left the ensemble mid-bloom, so it may be grown again; cannot-grow-on from a nurse that grows only from new words; empty-prompt for a prompt with neither words nor a graft
FIELD subtype string?
DOC the cell's own word for what broke
FIELD nectar any?
DOC what the bloom took before it broke off

CHI pulse
DOC a cell's life, and headroom
EMITS nurse
HEARS forager humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD kind pulse-kind
DOC the moment in the cell's life
FIELD pid int?
DOC the cell's process
FIELD headroom headroom?
DOC the nurse's headroom after this
FIELD cell string?
DOC on cell-ready: the cell's id
FIELD model string?
DOC on cell-ready: its model
FIELD tools [any]?
DOC on cell-ready: its tools

CHI scout
DOC send a scout out
EMITS nurse
HEARS forager
FIELD task string?
DOC what the scout is sent to do
FIELD tools [any]?
DOC what it may reach

CHI tendril-reach
DOC a tendril reaching
EMITS nurse forager
HEARS forager builder attendant
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD callId string
DOC minted by the reacher; the result carries it back
FIELD name string
DOC the tool
FIELD args any?
DOC its input, as the tool's schema says
FIELD cwd string?
DOC on a bash reach to a builder: where its shell starts; its host's home directory when absent

CHI tendril-meta
DOC what a tendril carries besides its result
EMITS nurse
HEARS forager
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD callId string?
DOC the reach it is about
FIELD name string?
DOC the tool
FIELD metadata any?
DOC what it carries

CHI tendril-info
DOC a tendril that already came back, told whole, for showing only
EMITS nurse
HEARS forager
FIELD callId string
DOC the reach, already answered
FIELD name string?
DOC the tool
FIELD args any?
DOC what it was given
FIELD result any?
DOC what came back
FIELD isError bool?
DOC it failed

CHI echo
DOC delivery ack for a rid
EMITS humd bee
HEARS bee humd
FIELD ok bool
DOC the tone under this rid was taken
FIELD error string?
DOC why not, when ok is false

CHI perf-mark
DOC a timing measurement — measured both ways
EMITS bee humd
HEARS bee humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD at int?
DOC when, ms UTC
FIELD note string?
DOC what was measured

CHI log
DOC structured log forwarding
EMITS bee humd
HEARS bee humd
FIELD level string?
DOC trace, debug, info, warn or error
FIELD message string?
DOC the line
FIELD fields any?
DOC structured fields; from humd, an advisory: fields.advisory is its code

CHI drone
DOC drone heartbeat
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD health string
DOC the drone's own word for how it is
FIELD rhythm_ms uint?
DOC ms between beats
FIELD pending_echoes [any]?
DOC rids sounded and not yet echoed
FIELD load drone-load?
DOC what it is carrying

CHI drone-retrofit
DOC drone swallow + retry signal
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD sigil string?
DOC the sigil to retry
FIELD reason string?
DOC why

# Between humds. A humd sounds these to its peers, or to itself.

CHI peer-add
DOC register a peer humd, once its hello is verified: a humd's ensemble tells its own kernel
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
FIELD humd_id string
DOC the peer, in hex
FIELD hints [any]?
DOC where it may be reached

CHI peer-remove
DOC drop a peer humd
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
FIELD humd_id string
DOC the peer, in hex

CHI attach
DOC observe a sid hosted on another humd: its reply tones then fan out to the observer too
EMITS forager
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD hearOnly bool?
DOC hear the sid's tones without taking part

CHI detach
DOC stop observing a sid
EMITS forager
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble

CHI wane-sync
DOC reconcile wane after a partition heals: each side sends its snapshot, and each merges by max
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD snapshot {uint}
DOC sigil to wane

CHI gossip-publish
DOC ensemble-wide gossip: deduped on msg_id, dispatched by topic, re-fanned to every other peer
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD topic string
DOC what the message is about; subscribers listen by it
FIELD payload any
DOC the message
FIELD from string?
DOC the originator
FIELD msg_id string
DOC minted once per publish by the originator, never derived from the rid or the payload

CHI kad-find-node
DOC Kademlia FIND_NODE: ask a peer for the peers it knows closest to a target
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD query_id string
DOC matches the answer to its query
FIELD target string
DOC a hid, in hex

CHI kad-find-node-resp
DOC Kademlia FIND_NODE answer: up to K peers closest to the target
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD query_id string
DOC the query it answers
FIELD closest [any]
DOC HumdAddrs, closest in XOR distance to the target

CHI backfill
DOC replay thehum's chi-log for an author, from a sequence number
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD author string
DOC a hid
FIELD from int?
DOC the first sequence number wanted

CHI backfill-event
DOC one event of a backfill
EMITS humd
HEARS humd
CARRIES ensemble
FIELD event any
DOC the event, as thehum logged it

# Shapes nested in bodies.

SHAPE headroom
DOC how many more cells a nurse can take
FIELD freeSlots uint
DOC cells it can still take
FIELD totalSlots uint
DOC cells it can hold at most

SHAPE petal
DOC one unit of content: in a prompt's content, and in a graft
FIELD kind petal-kind
DOC which unit of content it is
FIELD text string?
DOC words: of a text, sepal or thorn petal
FIELD grain grain?
DOC of a pollen petal
FIELD callId string?
DOC of a tendril or grasp petal: the reach
FIELD name string?
DOC of a tendril petal: the tool
FIELD args any?
DOC of a tendril petal: its input
FIELD result any?
DOC of a grasp petal: what came back
FIELD isError bool?
DOC of a grasp petal: it failed
FIELD propolis string?
DOC sealing a sepal petal
FIELD source any?
DOC of a waggle petal: where the words came from
FIELD brix any?
DOC of a brix petal: how likely each token was
FIELD bouquet [any]?
DOC of a bouquet petal: the candidates

SHAPE grain
DOC a grain of media
FIELD kind string
DOC image, audio or file
FIELD mediaType string
DOC its media type, image/png and the like
FIELD data string?
DOC the bytes, inline
FIELD url string?
DOC or where to fetch them

SHAPE prune
DOC cut the unlikely tail
FIELD p float?
DOC the nucleus: the likeliest tokens whose likelihood sums to p
FIELD k uint?
DOC the k likeliest tokens

SHAPE tendrils
DOC how a bloom reaches its tendrils
FIELD reach string?
DOC auto, none, required, or a tendril's name
FIELD parallel bool?
DOC whether the bloom may reach several at once

SHAPE sepal
DOC how much the cell reasons first
FIELD effort string?
DOC how hard, on the cell's own scale
FIELD budget uint?
DOC how many tokens of reasoning

SHAPE bloom
DOC one bloom of a graft: what its prompt carried, and what grew
FIELD content [petal]?
DOC what its prompt carried
FIELD grew [petal]?
DOC what grew

SHAPE model
DOC a model, and the hive that grows it
FIELD id string
DOC the model, as its hive names it
FIELD hive string
DOC the hive that grows it

SHAPE drone-load
DOC what a drone is carrying
FIELD active_sigils uint?
DOC sigils with a bloom open
FIELD inflight_tools uint?
DOC tendrils reaching
FIELD tokens_burned uint?
DOC nectar so far

# Kinds: closed sets of strings a field is drawn from.

KIND role
DOC the one job a bee does, set when its hive enters it
VALUE forager
DOC opens blooms, bringing the outside world into the thrum
VALUE nurse
DOC grows blooms in its cells; all inference is nursing
VALUE builder
DOC changes the world: runs what a bloom composes on its host, through `bash`
VALUE attendant
DOC serves the fixed, named tools in its hello's `tools`, and the `scent` of the models its hello's `models` name, and nothing else

KIND petal-kind
DOC which unit of content a petal is
VALUE text
DOC words, in `text`
VALUE tendril
DOC a brokered tool call: `callId`, `name`, `args`; its input grows as `sap`
VALUE grasp
DOC what a tendril came back with: `callId`, `result`, `isError`
VALUE pollen
DOC a grain of media: `grain` with its `kind` (image, audio, file), `mediaType`, and `data` or `url`
VALUE sepal
DOC the cell's reasoning, in `text`, sealed by `propolis` so it can carry into the next bloom
VALUE waggle
DOC where a petal's words came from: `source`
VALUE thorn
DOC the cell declining, or a filter acting: `text` says why
VALUE brix
DOC how likely each token was: `brix`
VALUE bouquet
DOC several candidate petals for one prompt: `bouquet`

KIND pulse-kind
DOC a moment in a cell's life
VALUE cell-spawned
DOC process created
VALUE cell-ready
DOC brooded: accepting prompts, its id, model and tools known
VALUE cell-idle
DOC the bloom wilted, no listeners
VALUE cell-died
DOC process exited
VALUE cell-evicted
DOC killed to make room

# Patterns: the figures tones make together.

PATTERN attunement
DOC a bee's hello and humd's verdict: humd echoes the hello's rid, then breathes to admit the bee, or echoes ok false under the same rid to refuse it; a refusal is final
OPEN hello
STEP echo
CLOSE breath echo

PATTERN bloom
DOC one turn of conversation: a prompt opens it, each unfurl grows one petal, and it closes when it wilts or breaks off; a cancel closes it early, as a wilt whose reason is cancel
KEY sid
OPEN prompt
STEP unfurl cancel
CLOSE wilt error

PATTERN tendril
DOC a tool reaching and grasping, within a bloom or straight from a forager to an attendant
KEY callId
OPEN tendril-reach
STEP tendril-meta
CLOSE tendril-result error

# Advisories: humd refuses what it must and advises on the rest. An
# advisory reaches a bee as a log tone whose fields.advisory is one of
# these codes; hum's client raises some itself before a tone leaves the bee.

ADVISORY undeclared-key
BY client humd
DOC a tone carries keys the thrum does not declare for its chi

ADVISORY unknown-chi
BY client
DOC a tone's chi is not in the thrum

ADVISORY not-a-tone
BY client
DOC a line from the bee is not a JSON object with a chi, and was dropped

ADVISORY client-owned
BY client
DOC the bee set a hello field the client owns, and it was ignored

ADVISORY tone-refused
BY client
DOC humd refused a tone under a rid the client gave it

ADVISORY dropped-while-away
BY client
DOC tones sent while humd was away were dropped

ADVISORY proto-drift
BY humd
DOC the bee speaks another minor version of the thrum

ADVISORY reconnect-storm
BY humd
DOC the bee said hello 10 times within 10 minutes

ADVISORY did-not-return
BY humd
DOC the bee was nestled when humd stopped and had not come back 2 minutes after humd started

ADVISORY cwd-not-hum
BY humd
DOC a prompt's `cwd` is not a `hum://` address, and was dropped
